   *   *   *   *   *
.SS __SYSTEM_64_BIT__
.IP
.EX
#define __SYSTEM_64_BIT__
.EE
.PP
This macro indicates that the target architecture of the system is
64\-bit.
.PP
If this macro is defined, the other \f[CR]32\f[R], \f[CR]16\f[R], and
\f[CR]8\f[R] bit macros might not be defined.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS __SYSTEM_32_BIT__
.IP
.EX
#define __SYSTEM_32_BIT__
.EE
.PP
This macro indicates that the target architecture of the system is
32\-bit.
.PP
If this macro is defined, the other \f[CR]64\f[R], \f[CR]16\f[R], and
\f[CR]8\f[R] bit macros might not be defined.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS __SYSTEM_31_BIT__
.IP
.EX
#define __SYSTEM_31_BIT__
.EE
.PP
This macro indicates that the target architecture supports 31\-bit
addressing (IBM System/390).
.PP
\f[CR]__SYSTEM_32_BIT__\f[R] is also defined for this target.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS __SYSTEM_16_BIT__
.IP
.EX
#define __SYSTEM_16_BIT__
.EE
.PP
This macro indicates that the target architecture of the system is
16\-bit.
.PP
If this macro is defined, the other \f[CR]64\f[R], \f[CR]32\f[R], and
\f[CR]8\f[R] bit macros might not be defined.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS __SYSTEM_8_BIT__
.IP
.EX
#define __SYSTEM_8_BIT__
.EE
.PP
This macro indicates that the target architecture of the system is
8\-bit.
.PP
If this macro is defined, the other \f[CR]64\f[R], \f[CR]32\f[R], and
\f[CR]16\f[R] bit macros might not be defined.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS __SYSTEM_BIT__
.IP
.EX
#define __SYSTEM_BIT__
.EE
.PP
This macro is defined as \f[CR]64\f[R], \f[CR]32\f[R], \f[CR]16\f[R], or
\f[CR]8\f[R], depending on the architecture.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS __HAS_128_BIT__
.IP
.EX
#define __HAS_128_BIT__
.EE
.PP
Defined if the compiler provides a native 128\-bit integer type (i.e.,
\f[CR]__int128\f[R] is available and its size is 16 bytes).
.PP
This macro indicates type support, not the system\(aqs architecture.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS __HAS_64_BIT__
.IP
.EX
#define __HAS_64_BIT__
.EE
.PP
Defined if the implementation supports 64\-bit integer types (e.g.,
\f[CR]long long\f[R]), even on 16\-bit or 32\-bit systems.
.PP
This macro indicates language/compiler support for 64\-bit integers, not
that the architecture is 64\-bit.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS __HAS_512_BIT_VECTOR__
.IP
.EX
#define __HAS_512_BIT_VECTOR__
.EE
.PP
Defined if the target architecture and compiler provide native 512\-bit
SIMD vector types (e.g., AVX\-512) or ARM SVE 512\-bit.
.PP
Indicates availability of 512\-bit vector registers/types, not general
vectorization capability.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS __HAS_256_BIT_VECTOR__
.IP
.EX
#define __HAS_256_BIT_VECTOR__
.EE
.PP
Defined if the target architecture and compiler provide native 256\-bit
SIMD vector types (e.g., AVX/AVX2) or ARM SVE 256\-bit.
.PP
Indicates availability of 256\-bit vector registers/types.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS __HAS_128_BIT_VECTOR__
.IP
.EX
#define __HAS_128_BIT_VECTOR__
.EE
.PP
Defined if the target architecture and compiler provide native 128\-bit
SIMD vector types (e.g., SSE, NEON).
.PP
Indicates availability of 128\-bit vector registers/types.
